::heading level=1 id=title
A Notepad for Code
::end

::paragraph id=lead
This document is not describing a program. It **is** one. The code blocks below run on your machine, pull in real libraries, and store what they produced right back into this file — so the next person to open it sees the results, not just the source.
::end

::heading level=2 id=numbers
Numbers, computed here
::end

::paragraph id=numbers-lead
`dx run showcase.dx` executes this block with `numpy`, installed on demand.
::end

::code id=stats lang=python run deps=numpy
import numpy as np

latency_ms = np.array([12, 18, 9, 44, 15, 21, 13, 120, 17, 11])

print(f"requests   {latency_ms.size}")
print(f"p50        {np.percentile(latency_ms, 50):.1f} ms")
print(f"p95        {np.percentile(latency_ms, 95):.1f} ms")
print(f"worst      {latency_ms.max()} ms")
::end

::output id=stats-output for=stats status=ok hash=b1323d9097e9ba05
requests   10
p50        16.0 ms
p95        85.8 ms
worst      120 ms
::end

::heading level=2 id=picture
A picture, drawn here
::end

::paragraph id=picture-lead
A block that declares `format=svg` has its output rendered as a drawing instead of quoted as text. That is what lets an agent look at a chart and reason about the shape of the data — rather than imagining it from the code that would have produced it.
::end

::code id=chart lang=python run deps=numpy format=svg
import numpy as np

latency_ms = [12, 18, 9, 44, 15, 21, 13, 120, 17, 11]
width, height, pad = 720, 240, 32
scale = (height - 2 * pad) / max(latency_ms)
step = (width - 2 * pad) / (len(latency_ms) - 1)

points = " ".join(
    f"{pad + index * step:.1f},{height - pad - value * scale:.1f}"
    for index, value in enumerate(latency_ms)
)
dots = "".join(
    f'<circle cx="{pad + i * step:.1f}" cy="{height - pad - v * scale:.1f}" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/>'
    for i, v in enumerate(latency_ms)
)

print(f'''<svg viewBox="0 0 {width} {height}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Request latency">
  <line x1="{pad}" y1="{height - pad}" x2="{width - pad}" y2="{height - pad}" stroke="#8894a4" stroke-width="1"/>
  <polyline points="{points}" fill="none" stroke="#6cb0ff" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  {dots}
  <text x="{pad}" y="{pad - 8}" fill="#8894a4" font-family="monospace" font-size="13">request latency (ms)</text>
</svg>''')
::end

::output id=chart-output for=chart status=ok hash=6866343b9f5101b3 format=svg
<svg viewBox="0 0 720 240" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Request latency">
  <line x1="32" y1="208" x2="688" y2="208" stroke="#8894a4" stroke-width="1"/>
  <polyline points="32.0,190.4 104.9,181.6 177.8,194.8 250.7,143.5 323.6,186.0 396.4,177.2 469.3,188.9 542.2,32.0 615.1,183.1 688.0,191.9" fill="none" stroke="#6cb0ff" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <circle cx="32.0" cy="190.4" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="104.9" cy="181.6" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="177.8" cy="194.8" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="250.7" cy="143.5" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="323.6" cy="186.0" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="396.4" cy="177.2" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="469.3" cy="188.9" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="542.2" cy="32.0" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="615.1" cy="183.1" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/><circle cx="688.0" cy="191.9" r="4" fill="#6cb0ff"/>
  <text x="32" y="24" fill="#8894a4" font-family="monospace" font-size="13">request latency (ms)</text>
