::end

::heading level=2 id=how
How to use it
::end

::numbered-list id=steps
- Write prose and code in plain text. A .dx file is readable with `cat` and diffable in a pull request.
- Mark a code block `run` and list any libraries it needs with `deps`.
- Run `dx run showcase.dx`. Unchanged blocks are skipped, so re-running is nearly free.
- Open the file in VS Code to read it as a page, or `dx png showcase.dx` to get an image of it.
::end

::heading level=2 id=agents
What an agent sees
::end

::bulleted-list id=agent-tools
- `dx_view` returns this page as an image — the chart above arrives as a picture.
- `dx_outline` maps the blocks so only the relevant section has to be fetched.
- `dx_run` executes the code and reports what each block produced.
- `dx_edit` changes one block by id without rewriting the rest of the file.
::end

::quote id=closing
The point is not that a document can hold code. It is that a document can hold the *result* — checked in, reproducible, and visible to whoever opens it next.
::end
